From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:02:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Partial-cell fix on by default (Oceananigans.jl#6533);
 bathymetry and bottom-cell options

partial_cell_fix.jl: Oceananigans.jl PR #6533 (issue #6532) as a run-time override until it is released
(it is on Oceananigans 0.118; NumericalEarth is on 0.117). With partial bottom cells, WENOVectorInvariant lets
jets grow in thin bottom cells next to thicker ones: the 100 km smoke test had 0.9 m/s at 2450 m in the
partial bottom cell of the Atlantic open side (Labrador Sea). Where the wet thickness of the bottom cells
around a velocity face changes by more than 1 %, momentum is advected in flux form; elsewhere nothing
changes, and whole-cell grids are untouched. [grid] partial_cell_fix = true (default).

[grid] bathymetry = "GEBCO2026" (default, as before) | "ETOPO" | "GLORYS" (GLORYS's own sea floor,
glorys_bathymetry.jl from fjp/nested), and [grid] bottom = "partial" (default, as before) | "full".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
